What is Titanium 64 Alloy Powder?
Titanium 64 Alloy Powder is a high-performance material composed primarily of titanium with 6% aluminum and 4% vanadium (Ti-6Al-4V), along with trace elements. Known for its exceptional strength-to-weight ratio, corrosion resistance, and biocompatibility, this alloy powder is manufactured through advanced processes like gas atomization and plasma rotating electrode methods. The powder exhibits uniform particle size distribution and spherical morphology, making it ideal for additive manufacturing and powder metallurgy applications.

This specialized powder form enables the production of complex, high-strength components across critical industries including aerospace, medical implants, and automotive sectors. Its unique properties allow manufacturers to create lightweight yet durable parts that withstand extreme conditions, from jet engine components to orthopedic implants.

